Integration test for prolongation_type="vecpot", the flux-preserving
prolongation of an edge-staggered vector potential.  See PROLONG_A.md at the
top of the repository for the construction and its verification status.

The headline check is "pure gauge": initial data is the exact discrete gradient
of a smooth scalar, so B vanishes to machine precision on the coarse level.
The refinement boundary is what is being tested -- the prolongation must leave
B zero in the fine level's ghost zones.  Interpolating A_i with a generic
stencil would not; producing no magnetic field from a pure gauge field is the
property that distinguishes this operator.

  test/puregauge.par     max |Bvec_*| must stay at round-off

The "smooth" initial condition has a nonzero B and is there for convergence and
for flux conservation across the refinement boundary.

divB is identically zero for any edge-staggered A, prolonged or not, so it
checks this thorn's own bookkeeping rather than the operator.

The same properties are checked without a toolkit build, in more detail, by
CarpetX/test/unit/; run ./CarpetX/test/unit/run.sh.
